From c9f30f76dde4520e65cf9a200a50addaaabd9c69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allcodernet <67543055+allcodernet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 22:12:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/45] decide: prefix slots, prefix cache, temperature flag,
 sampler detach, fault hook

The engine keeps up to 8 prefix slots, slot v in seq_base + v (spec
6.1). A request with K catalogue variants (K = 1 until debiasing
lands) uses slots 0..K-1; state c owns the K*(1+B) ids from
seq_base + K + c*K*(1+B), variant v's trunk at offset v*(1+B) with its
branches after it, so K = 1 is the old layout. spr is
(decide_seqs - K) / (K*(1+B)); spr = 0 is the 400 budget error with the
single message of spec 7.3.

Every budget check runs before a slot changes. Then slots >= K are
evicted, every id from seq_base + K is cleared, and slots 0..K-1 are
filled: resident, restored from the cache, or decoded. At the end of
every request, on errors too (a try/catch around the whole request,
because the second rc == 1 is thrown outside the per-round catch),
slots >= 1 are evicted and the ids above slot 0 are cleared, so only
slot 0 holds cells between requests.

--decide-prefix-cache N (0-16, default 8) is an LRU of host snapshots
(llama_state_seq_get/set_data, flags 0) with at most N entries and
2 GiB. Evicting a valid slot whose hash is not cached stores its
snapshot; filling a slot restores a cached snapshot and checks the
set_data result and seq_pos_max, else clears the slot, drops the entry
and decodes. Responses add timings.prefix_ms (part of prefill_ms),
usage.cached_tokens (resident or restored prefix tokens) and
engine.prefix_cache {capacity, entries, hits, misses}; info adds
prefixes (every slot that holds cells), prefix_cache {capacity,
entries, bytes} and temperature.

--decide-temperature T (0.05-20, default 1.0) is registered like
--decide-seqs and copied into engine_config. Until the engine applies
it, a value other than 1 turns every request into the 500 "not
implemented yet: temperature" guard (decide-api reads engine::config()).

Hardening (spec 9): the engine detaches any backend sampler from its
sequences at construction (llama_set_sampler(ctx, s, nullptr)).
LLAMA_DECIDE_FAULT=rc1 makes the first branch-phase decode of the first
attempt of every round return 1 without decoding; rc1-twice does it for
both attempts of the first round after construction (a 500); rc1-phase1
is accepted for the "after" phases. timings.retries counts retried
rounds. llama-decide --help documents the variable.
